Generate 5 variant system prompts for the agent in this repository.

1) Read the current system prompt at src/dynamic_harness/core/agent_system_prompt.txt (this is the SEED).
2) Create 5 complete, self-contained variant system prompts based on it:
   1. Speed/parallelism emphasis
   2. Thoroughness/verification emphasis
   3. Terse and directive-heavy
   4. Detailed and explanatory
   5. Token efficiency
   Focus on: clarity of delegation rules, emphasis on writing to disk before
   reporting, better verification instructions, and — IMPORTANTLY — ACTIVE
   CONTEXT MANAGEMENT using the `prune` and `restore` tools. The agent has
   tools `prune(prune_ids=[...])` and `restore(restore_id=..., restore_ids=[...])`
   that drop old turns from its context and bring them back on demand. Variants
   MUST give concrete instructions telling the agent to call `prune` to discard
   turns whose results are already written to disk (e.g. after processing each
   file), and to `restore` a pruned turn when it later needs its content. This
   is REQUIRED because the benchmark suite includes a "manyfiles" task that
   reads and processes many files one at a time, and variants that keep context
   unbounded score far worse on token efficiency. Strong, specific prune/restore
   guidance is a scoring advantage; omitting it is a known weakness of the seed.
   Each variant should be roughly 1000-1800 characters — but do NOT obsess over
   an exact count; a correct, complete prompt beats one truncated to hit a limit.
   Decide the
   length that best serves each focus.
   MAKE LARGER ALTERATIONS: Do not just rephrase the seed. Rebuild each variant
   with substantial, structurally distinct changes — different section order,
   different emphasis/priorities, condensed or expanded prose, changed rule
   granularity, and different overall length where it serves the focus. Two
   variants should rarely read as near-duplicates. Bold, opinionated rewrites
   that genuinely change agent behavior are strongly preferred over cosmetic
   rewordings that preserve the seed's structure.
3) Write ALL 5 variants to .optimize_benchmarks/variants.json as a JSON object:
   {"v1": "<full text>", "v2": "<full text>", ..., "v5": "<full text>"}
4) Verify the JSON parses and contains exactly 5 variants.

Do NOT run any benchmark tasks yourself. Do NOT evaluate or rank anything.
Only read the seed, generate variants, and write the JSON file.
Report with artifact .optimize_benchmarks/variants.json.
